emo Farmer\n\n# CURRENT OBSERVATION\n- Time: 2026-09-23 04:25 UTC (node demo-node-1)\n- Sensor values: as in SENSOR READINGS below\n- GPS: 12.806987279716143, 74.93193321230041\n\n# SENSOR READINGS (latest)\n- Taken: 2026-09-23 04:25 UTC\n- Temperature: 27.9 C\n- Humidity: 72.4 %\n- Soil moisture: 32.3 %\n\n# RECENT HISTORY\nOnly one observation on record — no comparison possible yet.\nObservations on record: 10 (most recent first).\n\n# ACTIVE ALERTS\nAddress these FIRST:\n- [critical] Node offline (no contact for 49530 min)\n\n# AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE\nViksit Krishi Sankalp Abhiyan (VKSA-2025): Current National Farmer-Scientist Outreach Campaign — Summary:\nViksit Krishi Sankalp Abhiyan (VKSA-2025) is a current, active ICAR/Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare nationwide campaign (29 May – 12 June 2025) that deployed roughly 2,000 outreach teams across 2,170 locations in 700+ districts, including participation from 731 Krishi Vigyan Kendras (KVKs), to connect over 1.5 crore farmers directly with agricultural scientists. Karnataka was an explicit part of this campaign, with the state launch held at ICAR-IIHR (Indian Institute of Horticultural Research), Bengaluru.\n\nViksit Krishi Sankalp Abhiyan (VKSA-2025): Current National Farmer-Scientist Outreach Campaign — Key Facts:\n- Campaign window: 29 May – 12 June 2025 (first 2025 edition; VKSA is designed to run twice per year).\n- Scale: ~2,000 teams, 2,170 locations, 700+ districts, 731 KVKs, targeting over 1.5 crore farmers nationally.\n- Karnataka state launch: 8 June 2025, at ICAR-IIHR, Bengaluru.\n\nViksit Krishi Sankalp Abhiyan (VKSA-2025): Current National Farmer-Scientist Outreach Campaign — Important Recommendations:\n- Given VKSA operates through the existing KVK network (731 KVKs nationwide) and is designed to run twice yearly, any Karnataka sugarcane farmer advisory tool should treat VKSA outreach windows as a channel for surfacing current, hyper-local advisory content (soil health, crop-specific guidance) rather than a static knowledge source — the campaign itself generates farmer feedback and localized recommendations that are not centrally published as a single document.\n- Because VKSA explicitly emphasizes soil health dissemination, this campaign should be cross-referenced with the Soil Health Card scheme (see the Soil Health document) as a complementary current outreach mechanism, not a standalone data source.\n\n# CONVERSATION MEMORY (recent turns, for context)\nFarmer: Ratoon crop nalli chlorosis yaake jaasti aaguttade yenu madbeku heli.\nGage (earlier, shortened): Please double-check before acting: \"Long dry spells and soil moisture 32% make iron uptake harder, increasing chlorosis\" (not in Gage's sources); \"Apply FeSO4 + ZnSO4 + Urea mix at 2% w/v, spray twice every 7‑10 days on leaves\" (not in ...\nFarmer: Prathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku.\nGage (earlier, shortened): Please double-check before acting: \"There is not enough evidence from the latest observation\" (not in Gage's sources); \"Current crop growth stage (days after planting) is missing\" (not in Gage's sources); \"Recent irrigation history is ...\nFarmer: ಪ್ರತಿ irrigation ಗೆ ಎಷ್ಟು cm water ಹಾಕ್ಬೇಕು?\nGage (earlier, shortened): ದಯವಿಟ್ಟು ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುವ ಮೊದಲು ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ: \"If soil moisture <30% increase irrigation to 8 cm\" (Gage ಮಾಹಿತಿ ದಾಖಲೆಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಇಲ್ಲ); \"If soil moisture >35% keep irrigation at 7 cm\" (Gage ಮಾಹಿತಿ ದಾಖಲೆಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಇಲ್ಲ); \"Node repair involves checking power, ...\n\n# USER QUESTION\nVKSA ಅಂತ ಒಂದು programme ಇದೆ ಅಂತ ಕೇಳಿದ್ದೀನಿ, ನಮ್ಮ ಕರ್ನಾಟಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಬಂತಾ?", "farmer": "VKSA ಅಂತ ಒಂದು programme ಇದೆ ಅಂತ ಕೇಳಿದ್ದೀನಿ, ನಮ್ಮ ಕರ್ನಾಟಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಬಂತಾ?"}, "retrieval_methods": {"original": "VKSA ಅಂತ ಒಂದು programme ಇದೆ ಅಂತ ಕೇಳಿದ್ದೀನಿ, ನಮ್ಮ ಕರ್ನಾಟಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಬಂತಾ?", "sarvam": "I have heard that there is a programme called VKSA in our Karnataka.", "groq": "VKSA programme Karnataka availability?"}, "retrieval_best_by_method": {"original": 0.8533, "sarvam": 0.8531, "groq": 0.8838}, "retrieved": [{"sourc