ffice of the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare, established January 1965), in consultation with state governments and sugar industry associations, and finally approved by the CCEA.\n\nSugarcane Market Price: Fair and Remunerative Price (FRP) System — Summary:\nUnlike most agricultural commodities that rely purely on open-market price discovery, sugarcane in India is protected by a statutory minimum price mechanism — the Fair and Remunerative Price (FRP) — which sugar mills are legally required to pay farmers. The FRP is announced annually by the Cabinet Committee on Economic Affairs (CCEA) before each crushing season, based on Commission for Agricultural Costs and Prices (CACP) recommendations.\n\n# CONVERSATION MEMORY (recent turns, for context)\nFarmer: VKSA ಅಂತ ಒಂದು programme ಇದೆ ಅಂತ ಕೇಳಿದ್ದೀನಿ, ನಮ್ಮ ಕರ್ನಾಟಕದಲ್ಲಿ ಬಂತಾ?\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation:** - Active alert: [critical] Node offline (no contact for 49530 min). - Viksit Krishi Sankalp Abhiyan (VKSA‑2025) was launched in Karnataka on 8 June 2025 at ICAR‑IIHR, Bengaluru (as per agricultural knowledge). ...\nFarmer: ನಾನು ಯಾವ ಕಬ್ಬಿನ ತಳಿ ಹಾಕೊಬೇಕು ಅಂತ confuse ಆಗಿದೀನಿ, ಸರಿಯಾದ variety ಹೇಗೆ ಆರಿಸ್ಕೊಳಿ ಅಂತ ಹೇಳಿ.\nGage (earlier, shortened): ದಯವಿಟ್ಟು ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುವ ಮೊದಲು ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ: \"I don't have enough evidence from the latest observation\" (Gage ಮಾಹಿತಿ ದಾಖಲೆಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಇಲ್ಲ); \"Missing: current crop growth stage (days after planting)\" (Gage ಮಾಹಿತಿ ದಾಖಲೆಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಇಲ್ಲ); \"Missing: soil ...\nFarmer: Sir every time watering how much depth I give, any standard number?\nGage (earlier, shortened): Please double-check before acting: \"When soil moisture <30% the higher end (~8 cm) is advised\" (not in Gage's sources); \"When soil moisture >35% the lower end (~7 cm) is advised\" (not in Gage's sources); \"At 32.3% soil moisture the crop is ...\n\n# USER QUESTION\nWhat is the FRP for sugarcane this season and how soon must the mill pay?", "farmer": "What is the FRP for sugarcane this season and how soon must the m