ropriate to the delay: for a 2-week delayed monsoon onset, continue pre-monsoon irrigation intervals (8–10 days) with alternate-furrow application and trash mulching in ratoon; for longer delays (6–8 weeks), shift to a 10-day protective irrigation interval and watch for iron deficiency, which becomes likely under prolonged dry spells (foliar spray of 1% FeSO₄ + 0.5% ZnSO₄ + 2% urea is recommended in that case).\n\n# CONVERSATION MEMORY (recent turns, for context)\nFarmer: What is the FRP for sugarcane this season and how soon must the mill pay?\nGage (earlier, shortened): Please double-check before acting: \"There is not enough evidence from the latest observation\" (not in Gage's sources); \"The announced FRP amount for the current sugarcane crushing season is missing\" (not in Gage's sources). I don't have ...\nFarmer: Why are the leaves of my cane turning yellow?\nGage (earlier, shortened): Please double-check before acting: \"Node offline (no contact for 49,530 min)\" (not in Gage's sources); \"Yellowing of sugarcane leaves can be caused by nutrient deficiencies such as iron, magnesium, zinc; water stress; disease\" (not in ...\nFarmer: Is my soil too dry right now?\nGage (earlier, shortened): Please double-check before acting: \"Soil moisture reading of 32.3% is just above the typical lower‑limit threshold (~30%) for sugarcane.\" (not in Gage's sources); \"The soil is marginally moist, not yet critically dry, but close to the ...\n\n# USER QUESTION\nPrathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku.", "farmer": "Prathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku."}, "retrieval_methods": {"original": "Prathi irrigation ge eshtu cm neeru hakbeku.", "sarvam": "For each irrigation, the amount of water is measured in centimeters.Me, water should be added.", "groq": "sugarcane irrigation depth per cycle in centimeters"}, "retrieval_best_by_method": {"original": 0.8499, "sarvam": 0.8411, "groq": 0.9248}, "retrieved": [{"source": "irrigation/01_irrigation_water_management.md", "sec